{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}DemiEngine — Your game. Your engine.{% endblock %}
{% block description %}A Linux-first, open-source C++20 engine with Lua gameplay, a native editor, free packages, and experimental 3D animation and destruction.{% endblock %}
{% block styles %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="/home.css?v=1">{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
{% set source = 'https://github.com/JEAPI-DEV/DemiEngine/tree/main' %}
{% set docs = 'https://github.com/JEAPI-DEV/DemiEngine/blob/improvements_to_gamedesign' %}
<section class="hero engine-hero" aria-labelledby="engine-title">
  <div class="hero-content">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span></span> OPEN SOURCE / LINUX FIRST</div>
    <h1 id="engine-title">Your game.<br><em>Your engine.</em></h1>
    <p>Build with Lua. Shape scenes in the native editor. Keep the source in readable JSON. From 2D games to experimental 3D worlds you can break apart.</p>
    <div class="home-actions">
      <a class="button" href="{{ source }}">Get the engine ↗</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="{{ docs }}/docs/getting-started.md">Start building →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="engine-facts"><span>C++20 + Lua 5.4</span><span>Vulkan / bgfx</span><a href="{{ path('catalog') }}">{{ total }} free packages →</a></div>
  </div>
  <figure class="home-preview">
    <div class="preview-title"><span class="preview-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> DESTRUCTION WEAPON LAB <span>LIVE ENGINE CAPTURE</span></div>
    <img src="/images/destruction-lab.png" alt="DemiEngine's destruction lab: brick walls and a steel door, a hammer, tiled prototype surfaces and an evening sky." width="1280" height="720" fetchpriority="high">
    <figcaption><span>Real gameplay. Editable scenes.</span><a href="{{ docs }}/examples/destruction_weapons_3d_lab/README.md">Example instructions ↗</a></figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="engine-workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
  <div class="engine-section-heading"><div class="eyebrow muted">THE WORKFLOW</div><h2 id="workflow-title">Build it. Inspect it. Make it yours.</h2><p>The editor and command line work with the same project files. No hidden editor-only game state.</p></div>
  <div class="workflow-grid">
    <article><span class="feature-index">01 / AUTHOR</span><h3>A native workspace.</h3><p>Edit scenes, HUDs and prefabs. Use the Inspector, Undo/Redo, embedded Play and adjustable UI scaling.</p><a href="{{ docs }}/docs/editor.md">Explore the editor →</a></article>
    <article><span class="feature-index">02 / PLAY</span><h3>Explicit Lua gameplay.</h3><p>Import the services you need. Add typed script properties and reuse packages for movement, combat, UI and networking.</p><a href="{{ docs }}/docs/lua-modules.md">Read the Lua guide →</a></article>
    <article><span class="feature-index">03 / BREAK</span><h3>Destruction with a workflow.</h3><p>Author ordinary prefabs with fracture components. Jolt handles rigid bodies; Blast handles connected fragments. No NVIDIA GPU required.</p><a href="{{ docs }}/docs/fracture-authoring.md">Build a destructible wall →</a></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="engine-proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
  <div><div class="eyebrow">MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED</div><h2 id="proof-title">Put the engine<br>under load.</h2><p>The animation example can show 1,024 or 2,000 independently animated characters. Repeatable probes cover barrels, collisions and mixed workloads too.</p><a href="{{ docs }}/examples/animation_3d/README.md">Run the crowd demo →</a></div>
  <div class="proof-result"><span class="proof-number">2,000</span><h3>animated characters</h3><p>Recorded desktop reference: 1080p, Vulkan, RTX 3070 Ti Laptop, Release build. Frame time p95: 15.34 ms.</p><p class="proof-note">A scoped animation workload, not 2,000 AI agents or a universal FPS promise. Results vary with hardware and scene complexity.</p><a href="{{ docs }}/docs/3d-milestone-2-qualification.md">Hardware, settings &amp; qualification results ↗</a></div>
</section>

<section class="engine-packages" aria-labelledby="packages-title">
  <div class="engine-section-heading"><div class="eyebrow muted">LESS SETUP</div><h2 id="packages-title">Start with a package.</h2><p>Free code and assets, installed into your project. Versions stay in the lockfile; the game never contacts a registry.</p></div>
  <div class="package-spotlights">
    <a class="asset-spotlight" href="{{ path('package', {name: 'kenney.textures.prototype'}) }}">
      <img src="/images/kenney-prototype-preview.png" alt="Kenney's original preview of prototype grid textures in six colors." width="918" height="515" loading="lazy">
      <div><span class="feature-index">ASSETS / CC0</span><h3>Kenney Prototype Textures</h3><p>78 textures. Six colors. Ready-to-select asset IDs, with no manual importing.</p><span class="spotlight-link">See the textures →</span></div>
    </a>
    <div class="code-spotlight"><span class="feature-index">GAMEPLAY / BSD-3-CLAUSE</span><h3>Destruction tools for your game.</h3><p>Hammer timing, swept rockets, native impact adapters and proximity-based destruction streaming. Use the current development engine for these experimental APIs.</p><div class="home-command"><span>Inside your project directory</span><code>demi package add demi.gameplay.destruction@1.0.0</code></div><a href="{{ path('package', {name: 'demi.gameplay.destruction'}) }}">Explore the destruction package →</a><a class="all-packages" href="{{ path('catalog') }}">Browse all {{ total }} free packages ↗</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="engine-status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
  <div><div class="eyebrow muted">WHERE WE ARE</div><h2 id="status-title">An engine in active development.</h2></div>
  <div><h3>Available now</h3><p>Established 2D, isometric and UI workflows. Experimental 3D GPU skinning, Jolt physics, localized destruction, mesh denting and panorama backgrounds. Android support is qualified per feature and device.</p></div>
  <div><h3>What comes next</h3><p>HDR and tone mapping, metallic/roughness PBR, environment reflections and local reflection probes. Structural stress, large-world workflows and broader production qualification remain open.</p><a href="{{ docs }}/plan.md">Follow the roadmap →</a></div>
</section>
<section class="engine-resources" aria-label="Development resources"><a href="{{ docs }}/README.md">Current README ↗</a><a href="{{ docs }}/docs/streamed-destruction.md">Streaming &amp; damage saves ↗</a><a href="{{ docs }}/docs/rendering-and-effects.md">Rendering status ↗</a><a href="{{ docs }}/docs/shipping.md">Linux &amp; Android shipping ↗</a><a href="/publishing">Publish a package →</a></section>
{% endblock %}
